# Reframe backlog

The product and the command are `reframe`. Track work on the Reframe Backlog: https://github.com/users/sknampally/projects/1

Before changing code:

1. Use an open story on that project. The story has label `type:story` and a parent epic.
2. If no story covers the change, add one and parent it to an epic. Add an epic labeled `type:epic` when none fits.
3. Implement that story.
4. Run the tests that cover the change and report the story link, the result, and anything not verified.
5. Commit on a feature branch and open a pull request. Every change that reaches the repository goes through that pull request. The repository owner reviews and approves it. Do not push to main, and do not merge.

Cursor agents implement stories in this repo. Claude and Codex are model providers the `reframe` command can call during a run. They do not implement the backlog.
